ample of interface carpet led  by a real pioneer in the green business  movement CEO ray anderson and he had  this vision that companies would lease  carpet so we'd come in and lay the  carpet rent it to the company for five  years and come take it back recycle it  and bring them a new least carpet well  this business never literally got off  the ground it turned out no one wants to  lease carpet there are a whole lot of  accounting reasons why capital  write-offs are allowed for big  investments up front it never worked on  but Ray Anderson is a smart guy he's  moved away from that model and he's done  other things have been brilliantly  successful he sent his design crew out  into the forest and told them to be  inspired by nature yeah never thaw my  god this guy's a lunatic now why do we  have to have a CEO who's such a green  wacko they came back with an idea again  his core businesses floor tiles for the  office what turns out one of the huge  problems that's an environment and a  dollar problem is Miss laying carpet  failing the line patterns is the waste  having to tear things back up so they  developed a carpet tile line called  entropy which inspired by nature every  tile is different the patterns can be  mixed in that  in any way and this turns out to be a  huge game because you don't have to slow  down to align patterns which slows the  installation process a lot you don't  have waste by misalignment that you have  to tear up so you reduce the  environmental burden of waste and it  saves a lot of time and money so it's a  time money and environmental improvement  and this has become a huge bestseller  for them so one of the other lessons is  if at first you don't succeed you've got  to keep trying and companies are  increasingly finding that so the bottom  line and i'll close with is an answer  questions is it turns out that some of  the literature in this corporate  environmental strategy arena a lot of it  has been wrong it's been superficial and  when 